(\225  Middle Cerebral Artery \(MCA\): Contralateral hemiparesis and hemisensory loss affecting face and arm > leg, plus aphasia \(dominant hemisphere\) or hemineglect \(non-dominant hemisphere\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
60 593 Td
(\225  Anterior Cerebral Artery \(ACA\): Contralateral hemiparesis and hemisensory loss affecting the lower extremity > upper extremity/face, often with urinary incontinence and abulia.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.2 rg
60 571 Td
(\225  Posterior Cerebral Artery \(PCA\): Contralateral homonymous hemianopia with macular sparing, alexia without agraphia \(splenium of corpus callosum involvement\).) Tj
